hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"540","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Kisra will be destroyed, and there will be no Kisra after him, and Caesar will be destroyed, and there will be no Caesar after him. By the One in Whose hand is the life of Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him)! You will spend both of their treasures in the way of Allah."""
"541","Waki’ (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated with this chain a narration similar to the previous hadith."
"542","With this same chain: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""I neither give you anything from myself nor withhold from you; I am only a treasurer, and I give as I am commanded."""
